message:
Now I see it. `RemoveCodePageOfCapacity` calls `NumFreeLines(page)` which reads `page->info.lineIndex`. If a page in `pagesOpen` has uninitialized `lineIndex`, this is the MSAN read.

The key question is: how does a page with uninitialized `lineIndex` end up in `pagesOpen`?

Looking at `ReleaseCodePageNoTrack`:
```c
void  ReleaseCodePageNoTrack  (IM3Runtime i_runtime, IM3CodePage i_codePage)
{
    if (i_codePage)
    {
        IM3CodePage * list;
        bool pageFull = (NumFreeLines (i_codePage) < d_m3CodePageFreeLinesThreshold);
        ...
    }
}
```

This also calls `NumFreeLines`. So if `lineIndex` is uninitialized, this would also be an MSAN read. But the crash is in `AcquireCodePageWithCapacity`.

Wait - maybe the issue is different. Let me look at `AcquireCodePageWithCapacity`:

